- **Inputs:** Open `GF_ISOFile`, 1-based track number, 1-based description index, output slot. Consumes the handler type, the entry at `descriptionIndex-1`, and its display flags, justification, 48-bit colors, default box record, default style, font table or font name.
- **Outputs and errors:** GF_OK: `*out_desc` receives a descriptor built by `gf_odf_desc_new(GF_ODF_TX3G_TAG)` with display flags, default position, justification, background color, default style, and fonts populated from the entry. GF_BAD_PARAM on zero index, NULL slot, missing track or media, a handler other than TEXT/SUBT/MPEG_SUBT, missing entry, or a type other than TX3G/TEXT; GF_OUT_OF_MEM if construction fails.
- **Side effects and interactions:** QT `TEXT` entry: colors reduced from 48 bits via retained static `rgb_48_to_32`, style_flags zero, vert_justif −1, horiz_justif from textJustification, one font (duplicated name) only when named. `tx3g` entry: style, both justifications, and every font table record copied (names duplicated). `fonts` is one allocation of `font_count` records; each present `fontName` is heap-duplicated — the shape retained `gf_odf_del_tx3g` and `gf_odf_tx3g_write` consume.
- **Required sequencing and state:** Index, slot, track, handler, and entry checks precede allocation; entry type selects one populate path; then GF_OK. Read-only.
