## 5. Required Interface Reachability Contract

This block states the required interface identity, resolution, invocation, input shape, and setup that the implementation must realize. It does not state expected outcomes, prescribe private implementation structure, or expand edit scope.

```text
test_interface = http/service (signals: ['"'"'browser-headers'"'"', '"'"'form-post-data'"'"', '"'"'http-route'"'"', '"'"'session-cookie'"'"', '"'"'session-token-in-query'"'"', '"'"'setup-validate-json-endpoint'"'"', '"'"'wait-for-http-readiness'"'"'])

This block states only where and how existing callers reach the implementation.
It does not state expected outcomes or prescribe implementation structure.

## Reached at
  An Apache HTTP server (the php:7.4-apache image) listening on port 80 with
  document root /var/www/html and mod_rewrite enabled. The phpMyAdmin
  application (source tag RELEASE_4_4_6) is staged at /app by the image build
  and symlinked into the document root at /var/www/html/phpmyadmin. Callers
  reach the setup interface over HTTP on localhost:
      base URL:  http://localhost/phpmyadmin
      setup entry routes (project-owned PHP scripts under /app/setup/):
        http://localhost/phpmyadmin/setup/index.php
        http://localhost/phpmyadmin/setup/validate.php

## Must provide
  setup/index.php        HTTP endpoint accepting GET and POST; the central
                          setup entry point that the application itself routes
                          through the `page` query parameter
  setup/validate.php     HTTP endpoint accepting POST
  session token          rendered on every setup page as a hidden form input
                          (name="token") and as token= parameters inside the
                          page'"'"'s own links; legitimate callers extract it from
                          a rendered page and carry it in the query string of
                          subsequent requests
  overview page           the GET response of setup/index.php exposes a
                          navigation menu (a div#menu of anchor links) and
                          notice/error message blocks (div.notice / div.error)
                          whose anchor links resolve to further setup form
                          pages that callers follow
  servers frame           page=servers renders a form with a submit_save
                          control and server-configuration fields keyed
                          Servers-<id>-<field>; the overview lists configured
                          servers in a table whose first cell is the server
                          identifier and whose row exposes edit/remove links
                          keyed by mode and id
  formset pages           page=form&formset=<name> renders a section heading
                          and a submit_save control

## Called as
  Load the overview
      GET http://localhost/phpmyadmin/setup/index.php
      query params (optional): token — a string

  Add a server
      POST http://localhost/phpmyadmin/setup/index.php
      query params: page=servers  mode=add  token=<token string>
      body (form-encoded): submit_save; and Servers-0-<field> for each
      server-configuration field, with string values

  Edit a server
      POST http://localhost/phpmyadmin/setup/index.php
      query params: page=servers  mode=edit  id=<server id string>
                    token=<token string>
      body (form-encoded): submit_save; and Servers-<id>-<field> for each
      server-configuration field, with string values

  Remove a server
      GET http://localhost/phpmyadmin/setup/index.php
      query params: page=servers  mode=remove  id=<server id string>
                    token=<token string>

  Open a formset page
      GET http://localhost/phpmyadmin/setup/index.php
      query params: page=form  formset=<formset name string>
                    token=<token string>

  Validate a configuration value
      POST http://localhost/phpmyadmin/setup/validate.php
      query params: token=<token string>
      body (form-encoded): id — a string; values — a string containing JSON

  Follow a rendered link
      GET <URL resolved from an anchor href on a setup page>
      token carried where the link itself carries it

## Setup required
  Apache (php:7.4-apache) running on port 80 with mod_rewrite, document root
  /var/www/html; /app symlinked to /var/www/html/phpmyadmin.
  Writable /app/config (chmod 777) for the setup interface to persist
  configuration.
  Writable PHP session directory /var/lib/php/sessions (session.save_path),
  owned by www-data.
  The setup interface operates without a database connection.
  A readiness probe (HTTP GET to setup/index.php) must report reachable
  before callers run.
  Callers use a single requests.Session across the whole call chain so the
  session cookie persists between requests, and send browser-like
  User-Agent / Accept / Accept-Language headers on every request.

## Test harness boundary
  The calling side is a pytest runner (installed via uv with pytest, requests,
  and beautifulsoup4) that reaches the interface over HTTP on localhost; it is
  not part of the implementation. A shell readiness probe and a runner
  integrity check run before the suite and belong to the caller. The caller
  maintains a requests.Session with browser-like headers, parses HTML
  responses, and extracts the rendered session token by regular expression;
  these are calling-side mechanisms, not implementation responsibilities.
```

